From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Luma <engineering@projectluma.org>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 13:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Layer-shell surfaces in the Shell

The compositor's layer overlay group goes right above the windows in
uiGroup: overlay surfaces cover full-screen windows and stay under
everything the Shell draws. While the screen shield is up every layer
surface is hidden.

Grants for the four layer-shell capabilities are read from the permission
store (table luma, entry display-over-apps) before any app connects,
handed to Mutter and followed as they change. A surface Mutter fades for
covering too much of its output gets a name tag the Shell draws: the app's
icon and name in a pill just outside its top-left corner, in the LumaUI
overlay colour.

org.projectluma.LayerShell1 at /org/projectluma/LayerShell reports the
surfaces on screen, the apps showing overlays or faded, each app's grants,
use and offers, signals clamps and use, and sets a capability or stops an
app's overlays. The status indicator and the offer here are unstyled
placeholders built on it.
